Indeed apply the derivative product rule to the same matrix estimates;
the zero-, first- and second-derivative integrals are dominated by the
five-dimensional Gaussian integrals already used in the parent proof.
No extra phase singularity is introduced by a C^2 factor. A fixed gauge
